//! The write hooks of FileShare: they run, in the write's own transaction, the hook triggers the schema
//! declares for it and stage the events it declares with `on:`.
//!
//! Generated by metaphor-schema. Do not edit manually.
//!
//! They run around the repository write: `before` the triggers keyed `before_*`, after the row is written
//! and its lifecycle hooks have run, the `after_*` triggers in file order and then the declared events,
//! all before the commit. A failure of any of them rolls the write back, so a committed write always has
//! its events and the effects of its triggers. Delivery to subscribers is the outbox relay's, at least once.
